[{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/authors.html","id":null,"dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Authors","title":"Authors and Citation","text":"Miguel Serrano. Author, maintainer.","code":""},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/authors.html","id":"citation","dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Citation","title":"Authors and Citation","text":"Serrano M (2025). IndexNumberTools: Working Index Numbers. R package version 1.0, https://github.com/mserrano-ine/IndexNumberTools, https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/.","code":"@Manual{,   title = {IndexNumberTools: Working With Index Numbers},   author = {Miguel Serrano},   year = {2025},   note = {R package version 1.0, https://github.com/mserrano-ine/IndexNumberTools},   url = {https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/}, }"},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/index.html","id":"indexnumbertools","dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Working With Index Numbers","title":"Working With Index Numbers","text":"IndexNumberTools intends ease everyday work users producers index numbers providing functionalities like chain-linking, base shifting computing pyp indices.","code":""},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/index.html","id":"installation","dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Installation","title":"Working With Index Numbers","text":"","code":"# Install released version from CRAN install.packages(\"IndexNumberTools\")"},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/index.html","id":"getting-started","dir":"","previous_headings":"","what":"Getting started","title":"Working With Index Numbers","text":"’ll work example using Spanish GDP current prices, preloaded gdp_current, chain-linked volume (index), gdp_volume. can easily re-reference volume series change_ref_year().1 can also get series previous year prices gdp_volume get_pyp().2  Multiplying volume series mean current prices series reference year (2020), obtain GDP (chain-linked) constant prices. dividing GDP current prices GDP constant prices, derive chain-linked implicit deflator GDP. Using get_v_index() chain-linking result get_chain_linked(), get chain-linked value indices. , can verify identity V=P⋅QV = P\\cdot Q, , value index must equal product price volume indices.","code":"gdp_volume_2010 <- change_ref_year(gdp_volume, 2010) #> Time Series: #> Start = 2008  #> End = 2022  #> Frequency = 1  #>           2020      2010 #> 2008 104.90885 103.81798 #> 2009 100.95573  99.90596 #> 2010 101.05075 100.00000 #> 2011 100.40412  99.36010 #> 2012  97.52742  96.51331 #> 2013  96.13535  95.13571 #> 2014  97.59707  96.58224 #> 2015 101.56035 100.50430 #> 2016 104.52100 103.43417 #> 2017 107.54800 106.42969 #> 2018 110.12422 108.97913 #> 2019 112.28397 111.11642 #> 2020 100.00000  98.96018 #> 2021 106.68315 105.57383 #> 2022 113.27545 112.09758 gdp_pyp <- get_pyp(gdp_volume) ref_year_mean <- window(gdp_current,start = c(2020,1), end = c(2020,4)) |> mean() gdp_constant <- ref_year_mean * gdp_volume / 100 gdp_deflator <- gdp_current / gdp_constant * 100 gdp_value <- get_v_index(gdp_current) |> get_chain_linked(2020) dplyr::near(gdp_value, gdp_deflator * gdp_volume / 100) |> all() #> [1] TRUE"},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/IndexNumberTools-package.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"IndexNumberTools: Working With Index Numbers — IndexNumberTools-package","title":"IndexNumberTools: Working With Index Numbers — IndexNumberTools-package","text":"Chain-linking, base shifting, computing pyp indices, etc.","code":""},{"path":[]},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/IndexNumberTools-package.html","id":"author","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Author","title":"IndexNumberTools: Working With Index Numbers — IndexNumberTools-package","text":"Maintainer: Miguel Serrano miguel.serrano.martin@ine.es","code":""},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/aggr_rep_lag.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Aggregate, repeat and lag — aggr_rep_lag","title":"Aggregate, repeat and lag — aggr_rep_lag","text":"Helper function repeat aggregate annual value series period, possibly lag .","code":""},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/aggr_rep_lag.html","id":"ref-usage","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Usage","title":"Aggregate, repeat and lag — aggr_rep_lag","text":"","code":"aggr_rep_lag(x, fun = mean, k = 0)"},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/aggr_rep_lag.html","id":"arguments","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Arguments","title":"Aggregate, repeat and lag — aggr_rep_lag","text":"x (ts) time series fun (function) Aggregation function, mean default k (int) Units lag.","code":""},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/aggr_rep_lag.html","id":"value","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Value","title":"Aggregate, repeat and lag — aggr_rep_lag","text":"description","code":""},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/aggr_rep_lag.html","id":"details","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Details","title":"Aggregate, repeat and lag — aggr_rep_lag","text":"Applies aggregate.ts series get annual values repeats values every subyear period. k parameter passed stats::lag.","code":""},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/aggr_rep_lag.html","id":"ref-examples","dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Examples","title":"Aggregate, repeat and lag — aggr_rep_lag","text":"","code":"aggr_rep_lag(gdp_volume) |> plot()"},{"path":"https://mserrano-ine.github.io/IndexNumberTools/reference/apply_to_columns.html","id":null,"dir":"Reference","previous_headings":"","what":"Apply method to multivariate — apply_to_columns","title":"Apply method to multivariate 